1. Project Title

University Lost and Found Management System

2. Technical Feasibility

The project is technically feasible because the team can use available programming tools and 
technologies to develop the system. The system can be developed using web technologies and a database 
to store item information. The team can learn and use the required tools during the project.

3. Economic Feasibility

The project is economically feasible because most development tools are available for free.
The team can use existing computers and free software, so the project does not require a large budget.

4. Operational Feasibility

The system is expected to be useful for students and staff at Taibah University.
Users can report lost or found items and search for reported items. 
This can make the process more organized and save time.

5. Schedule Feasibility

The project can be completed within the course schedule if the team divides the tasks clearly and follows a work plan.
Each team member will be responsible for assigned tasks, and the team will review progress regularly.

6. Legal Feasibility

The system should protect users’ personal information and only collect the data needed for its purpose. 
The team should follow applicable privacy rules and obtain permission before using any university information or resources.

7. Final Recommendation

☑️ Proceed

The project is feasible because it can be developed using available tools and resources.
It can also help the university community manage lost and found items more easily.
The team should follow the project plan and consider user privacy during development.
